  "conclusion": "No reduced-precision decoder passes its stated limits. float16-storage fails 2 of 4 cases (rel L2 up to 0.41, log-mel up to 0.071); int8 and float16 compute fail every case (rel L2 0.6-1.4, log-mel 0.08-0.25). None improves warm speed or run-time memory; the only gain is decoder size (140, 65 and 121 MiB vs 236). float32 stays the only shipped bundle. The model's float32 sensitivity (a 1e-6 source perturbation moves output 1.5e-4) is the reason weight rounding at 1e-3 relative error is audible in waveform metrics.",
